{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Newly Constructed Multiple Dwellings Law rent-control exemption","requirement":"Newly constructed multiple dwellings are exempt from any local rent control ordinance for 30 years after construction is completed; rents subsidized by government funding may also be exempt from local rent control.","key_value":"30 years following completion of construction","coverage_conditions":"Newly constructed multiple dwellings; exemption lasts 30 years after completion of construction. Government-subsidized rents may also be exempt from local rent control.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"built_within_years","role":"exempt","years":30,"basis":"construction"}],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":["newly constructed multiple dwellings shall be exempt from any local rent control ordinances for a period of 30 years following completion of construction of the building"]},"exemptions":"Newly constructed multiple dwellings for 30 years after completion; rents subsidized by government funding may also be exempt from local rent control.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:42-84.5","quoted_span":"newly constructed multiple dwellings shall be exempt from any local rent control ordinances for a period of 30 years following completion of construction of the building","interaction":"State law sets no rent control; municipalities may adopt rent control ordinances, from which new multiple dwellings are exempt for 30 years.","relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Anti-Eviction Act notice and limit on rent increases","requirement":"A landlord may not raise the rent during a lease term; the old lease must be terminated and the tenant offered a new lease at the increased rent. The increase must not be unconscionable and must comply with municipal rent ordinances.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"Residential tenancies covered by the Anti-Eviction Act; rent increases must comply with any municipal ordinance governing increases.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"A landlord cannot raise the rent mid-lease term. The old lease must be terminated, and the new lease must have the increased rental payment.","interaction":"Rent increases must comply with municipal rent control ordinances where they exist.","relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"rent_increase_limits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Condominium or cooperative conversion rent increase prohibition","requirement":"When a building is converted to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership, a landlord may not increase rents to cover costs resulting solely from the conversion.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All tenants in a building converted to condominium, cooperative or fee simple ownership, whether or not eligible for protected tenancy.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Rent increases to cover the cost of new services or amenities are allowed.","penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.31","quoted_span":"If a building is converted to a condominium or cooperative form of ownership, or to fee simple ownership of units, rents may not be increased to cover cos ts resulting solely from the conversion","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"just_cause_eviction","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Anti-Eviction Act good-cause eviction requirement","requirement":"A residential landlord may evict or refuse to renew a lease only for good cause proved in court. Every cause except nonpayment of rent must be described in detail in a written Notice to Quit; a Notice to Cease may also be required.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All residential dwelling units; the Act protects blameless tenants in a housing shortage.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":null,"effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 2A:18-61.1","quoted_span":"No residential landlord may evict or fail to renew a lease, whether it is a written or an oral lease without good cause. The landlord must be able to prove in court that he has grounds for an eviction.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"security_deposits","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"New owner security deposit duty and withholding penalty","requirement":"A new owner must obtain the tenant's security deposit plus accrued interest from the former owner and is responsible for investing and returning it. Willfully withholding the deposit of a tenant receiving State or federal assistance carries a $500 to $2,000 civil penalty per offense.","key_value":"$500 to $2,000 per offense","coverage_conditions":"All residential security deposits; a special penalty applies where the tenant received State or federal financial assistance, including welfare or rental assistance.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":null,"coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":null,"penalty":"Civil penalty of not less than $500 or not more than $2,000 per offense, collected under the Penalty Enforcement Law; unlawful use of deposit monies is a disorderly persons offense punishable by a fine of $200 or up to 30 days' imprisonment, or both.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 46:8-21.1","quoted_span":"The landlord may be liable for a civil penalty of not less than $500 or not more than $2,000 for each offense.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.75,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-02","doc_id":"D067","jurisdiction":"NJ","category":"screening_restrictions","lifecycle":"enacted","title":"Law Against Discrimination source-of-lawful-income protection","requirement":"A landlord or rental agency may not refuse to rent or treat a person differently because of source of lawful income; the Law Against Discrimination requires equal treatment in the rental of housing.","key_value":null,"coverage_conditions":"All landlord-tenant relationships, except two-family owner-occupied dwellings, rooms in an owner- or resident-occupied single home, and single-sex or age-restricted housing as to familial status.","applicability":{"conditions":[{"type":"owner","role":"exempt","who":"owner-occupied two-family dwelling","unit_limit":2}],"per_tenancy":"Rooms in an owner- or resident-occupied single home; housing planned for and occupied by one sex or age-restricted housing, as it pertains to familial status.","coverage_quotes":["The law applies to all landlord -tenant relationships, except those involving two -family owner occupied dwellings, rooms in an owner or resident -occupied single home, and residences planned exclusively for and occupied by one sex, i.e. YMCA and age -restricted housing, as it pertains to familial status (N.J.S.A. 10:5-5(n))."]},"exemptions":"Two-family owner-occupied dwellings; rooms in an owner- or resident-occupied single home; residences planned for and occupied by one sex and age-restricted housing, as to familial status.","penalty":"Under the LAD, violators are subject to fines and penalties of up to $10,000 for a first offense.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"N.J.S.A. 10:5-12","quoted_span":"prohibits discrimination when selling or renting property and requires equal treatment in the sale or rental of housing regardless of race, creed, color, national origin, ancestry, sex, marital status, civil union status, domestic partnership status, familial status, affectional or sexual orientation, gender  identity or expression, mental and physical disability, nationality, or source of lawful income.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.65,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
{"packet_id":"D067-02","n_rules":6,"note":null}

